      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T18:55:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e GCC has a bug where it drops tokens after escaped quotes inside macros.\n\u003e That caused the static assert statment in HWY_BEFORE_NAMESPACE() and\n\u003e HWY_AFTER_NAMESPACE() to be dropped. Thus the extra semi warnings.\n\nIt would be good to add a reference to the bug. Was it fixed in GCC 16+?",
      "revId": "7915d069a50549c2cb94f272c0cfbd697b139110",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21ac6344_277d25f2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T18:56:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What a strange bug. Can we put this mitigation in Highway instead?\n\nI agree, it\u0027s probably better to start the discussion on the Highway side.",
      "parentUuid": "92589e64_34afe2d1",
      "revId": "7915d069a50549c2cb94f272c0cfbd697b139110",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81069d4f_533095c2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5960
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T19:48:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t find a bug related to this but there\u0027re similar ones that claim to be fixed in gcc 16 (https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d118838) but actually not this particular bug.\n\nI\u0027ve tried on godbolt.org (With -E option so it expands the macros) with gcc16 and it still complains.\n\nWith gcc 16.1:\n\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/6eshM7Gz9\n\nWith clang:\n\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/nW8n3Kxdc\n\nYou can see with gcc16.1, the static_assert() is completely dropped (line 12 in the right panel), leaving only the `;`. But clang has no issue.",
      "parentUuid": "21ac6344_277d25f2",
      "revId": "7915d069a50549c2cb94f272c0cfbd697b139110",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4af4ed6_4907cb53",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5960
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T20:15:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From Highway implementation here https://github.com/google/highway/blob/master/hwy/ops/set_macros-inl.h#L908\n\nIt does require a `;` after `HWY_BEFORE_NAMESPACE()` \n\nWe could remove that `static_assert()` upstream for gcc, but then we also need to have different versions of using this for gcc vs clang in libaom.",
      "parentUuid": "81069d4f_533095c2",
      "revId": "7915d069a50549c2cb94f272c0cfbd697b139110",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab142fbb_fb5ee938",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8084
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T17:54:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah this really resists mitigation within the macros: https://godbolt.org/z/svYMW5dex\n\nGCC seems to just forget to compile whatever comes next. It doesn\u0027t matter if it\u0027s valid C++ or anything.\n\nInstead of changing this in code, can we ignore -Wextra-semi on GCC 16 and friends?",
      "parentUuid": "d4af4ed6_4907cb53",
      "revId": "7915d069a50549c2cb94f272c0cfbd697b139110",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
